===============================PRACTICAL:Create a Responsive College Dashboard using HTML, CSS and BootstrapRun the webpage on Ubuntu 22.04 Virtual Machine using Vagrant===============================
--------------------------------------------------STEP 1: INSTALL REQUIRED SOFTWARE ON WINDOWS--------------------------------------------------
1. Install VirtualBoxhttps://www.virtualbox.org/
2. Install Vagranthttps://developer.hashicorp.com/vagrant/downloads
3. Restart computer after installation
--------------------------------------------------STEP 2: CREATE PROJECT FOLDER--------------------------------------------------
Open Command Prompt:
cd Desktopmkdir CollegeDashboardcd CollegeDashboard
--------------------------------------------------STEP 3: CREATE VAGRANT FILE--------------------------------------------------
Type:
vagrant init ubuntu/jammy64
This creates a Vagrantfile.
--------------------------------------------------STEP 4: START UBUNTU VIRTUAL MACHINE--------------------------------------------------
Type:
vagrant up
Wait for Ubuntu VM to download and start.
--------------------------------------------------STEP 5: LOGIN INTO UBUNTU VM--------------------------------------------------
Type:
vagrant ssh
Now you are inside Ubuntu Linux terminal.
--------------------------------------------------STEP 6: INSTALL APACHE WEB SERVER--------------------------------------------------
Inside Ubuntu VM type:
sudo apt updatesudo apt install apache2 -y
Start apache server:
sudo systemctl start apache2
Enable apache:
sudo systemctl enable apache2
Check status:
sudo systemctl status apache2
Press Q to exit status screen.
--------------------------------------------------STEP 7: GO TO WEB SERVER DIRECTORY--------------------------------------------------
Type:
cd /var/www/html
Check files:
ls
You will see index.html
--------------------------------------------------STEP 8: REMOVE DEFAULT PAGE--------------------------------------------------
Type:
sudo rm index.html
--------------------------------------------------STEP 9: CREATE NEW WEBPAGE--------------------------------------------------
Type:
sudo nano index.html
Paste the COMPLETE CODE below.
--------------------------------------------------STEP 10: COMPLETE HTML + CSS + BOOTSTRAP CODE--------------------------------------------------
